<item><title>Botswana projects P26.35 billion deficit as debt costs reach P38.46 billion</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-projects-p26-35-billion-deficit-as-debt-costs-52c202/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-projects-p26-35-billion-deficit-as-debt-costs-52c202/</guid><category>Botswana</category><description>The Ministry of Finance says the 2026/2027 shortfall is approximately nine percent of GDP, while public debt is expected to reach 45% by March 2027.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:11:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-projects-p26-35-billion-deficit-as-debt-costs-52c202/share.jpg" length="46007" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-projects-p26-35-billion-deficit-as-debt-costs-52c202/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
